          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            9. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a Topper to Fix a Sagging Mattress</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A topper follows the shape of the mattress beneath it, so it sinks into the same dip. Check for sag with a straight edge first. If the gap is more than about an inch and a half, the money is better spent toward a new mattress.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Choosing the Thickest, Softest Topper for Back Pain</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Thick, plush toppers let the hips sink below the shoulders, which many people with back pain find makes mornings worse. A thinner medium-firm or firm topper usually suits back and stomach sleepers better.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying Extra for Gel and Expecting a Cool Bed</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Gel and cooling covers make memory foam feel cooler at first touch, but the foam still warms up. If you sleep hot, latex or fiber is the more reliable fix.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring Foam Density</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Two toppers with the same thickness can last very different lengths of time. Look for the stated density, and treat a listing that hides it with some caution.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Skipping the Protector</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Most foam cores cannot be washed. Without a protector over the topper, sweat and spills soak straight into the foam, and that is usually the end of it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
